From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:40:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: don't describe tilebuffer-reading fragments as
 opaque (v6/v7)

KHR-GLES31.core.blend_equation_advanced.test_coherency.mixedSequence
fails on Mali-G31 (Bifrost v7.0): 44 fullscreen draws with different
advanced blend equations in one fragment job, each fragment reading the
previous result back from the tile buffer (KHR_blend_equation_advanced
is lowered into the fragment shader as a framebuffer fetch). The first
pixel is right but not all pixels agree, so the tile-buffer updates of
consecutive dependent fragments get out of order inside a tile. With a
glBlendBarrier between the draws (one fragment job per draw) the same
sequence passes, as do multiplySequence (7 draws) and the 86 other
blend_equation_advanced cases (one dependent draw per pixel).

The descriptors told the hardware that these fragments are opaque:

 * blend disabled + full colour mask gives pan_blend_is_opaque(), so the
   blend descriptor used MALI_BLEND_MODE_OPAQUE ("no tile-buffer read in
   there"), although the shader reads the tile buffer with LD_TILE;
 * the RSD overdraw alpha0/alpha1 hints were set ("alpha 0 is a no-op,
   alpha 1 fully overwrites"), although the result depends on the older
   fragments whatever the alpha is;
 * gl_nir_lower_blend_equation_advanced forces uses_sample_shading, and
   the partial RSD copied that straight into evaluate_per_sample, so the
   draws ran per-sample on a single-sampled framebuffer with multisample
   disabled (the v9+ JM path and panvk gate it on the sample count).

For fragment shaders whose outputs_read includes a render target: use
the fixed-function blend mode with the existing replace equation (when
the format is blendable and the equation fixed-function capable; opaque
mode stays otherwise), keep the alpha_zero_nop / alpha_one_store hints
off, and report no overdraw hints. Per-sample evaluation is now decided
at draw time from the framebuffer (msaa && (min_samples > 1 ||
shader sample shading)) and the shader's request is cleared from the
partial RSD. Everything else (forward pixel kill, early-ZS, dependency
waits) was already right: the compiled shader waits on slot 7 in its
first clause and the RSD carries shader_wait_dependency_7.

PAN_MESA_DEBUG=fbfetch_opaque,fbfetch_overdraw,persample_1x restore the
old descriptors one by one (debug A/B switches, default off). Verified
on the host with the panfrost drm-shim (fake G31): the 11 fbfetch draws
now use Fixed-Function mode, no overdraw hints, evaluate_per_sample
false; the board run is harness/runner-queue/15-gles-advblend.md.

Generated-by: LLM
